Z||000000||glava2876||10-30-2001||08:13 PM||||It took all summer, but I finally have my Fiero up and running -what a blast! The major problems are fixed -brakes, brake lines master cyl.,fuel pump, complete tune up etc., etc. on a car that sat for 12 years. Now I'm starting the minor problems and need some help. 1) I replaced the temperature sending unit, but the gauge still won't work. 2) In the engine compartment, on the clutch side near the fire wall, there are two green wires that couple together and become red, which ends at a broken rubber fitting -what can this be? 3) There is a black wire off the mainwiring that is ends the same way -at a broken rubber fitting.4)I have an electric trunk release, but no wiring runs to it -should go through a cavity in the deck lid?<BR>I'm thinking that 1-4 could be related? Lastly, even after having the front tires re-balanced, ther is still a vibration between 67 -72mph -what can this be? Thanks for any help anyone can provide. Thanks, Glen||||reg||10
Z||000001||Fierowrecker||10-30-2001||11:55 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by glava2876:<BR><B>It took all summer, but I finally have my Fiero up and running -what a blast! The major problems are fixed -brakes, brake lines master cyl.,fuel pump, complete tune up etc., etc. on a car that sat for 12 years. Now I'm starting the minor problems and need some help. 1) I replaced the temperature sending unit, but the gauge still won't work. 2) In the engine compartment, on the clutch side near the fire wall, there are two green wires that couple together and become red, which ends at a broken rubber fitting -what can this be? 3) There is a black wire off the mainwiring that is ends the same way -at a broken rubber fitting.4)I have an electric trunk release, but no wiring runs to it -should go through a cavity in the deck lid?<BR>I'm thinking that 1-4 could be related? Lastly, even after having the front tires re-balanced, ther is still a vibration between 67 -72mph -what can this be? Thanks for any help anyone can provide. Thanks, Glen</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>On your vibration problem, jack up the car and wiggle suspention components, see if your ball joints are worn, bad wheel bearings, etc...<BR>You need a wiring diagram for the other problems...<BR><P>------------------<BR>crash... The Fierowrecker<BR>         <IMG SRC="http://fiero.nl/uploads/crash_sig.jpg">        <IMG SRC="http://fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||fierohoho||10-31-2001||02:06 AM||||On the temp sending unit, if you ordered the part through GM and they looked up the part number on the computer it is wrong, they in all likelyhood gave you a sender marked fan switch on the box.<P>Check the part number they had against this one, #25036809<P>This part number is correct as I had this problem a couple years ago.<P>I got an old guy who looked the number up in the 22P book which is the right number, when I got the right sender I put the label in my toolbox, I also cross-checked it through my 22P book, sometimes you gotta love the old ways  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Let me know what comes up.<P>------------------<BR>'84 SE 2.5l<BR>'85 Coupe 2.5l now getting a 3800<BR>'86 SE 2.5l<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/lightbar.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||glava2876||10-31-2001||08:25 PM||||Thanks for the responses.<BR>1) I will check the suspension stuff, but the car has 38,000 original miles -which I know is true since I got the car from my mother, who bought it new. I inspected and packed the bearings when I had the brake rotors turned. Also, the car doesn't pull and it brakes straight.<BR>2) I bought the sending unit at a parts store -it is a Borg Warner "WT 3000 temperature sensor". Is there any way to cross reference the number an tell if they have the same issues as GM part numbers? Thanks, Glen<P>[This message has been edited by glava2876 (edited 10-31-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by glava2876 (edited 10-31-2001).]||||reg||10
Z||000004||fierohoho||10-31-2001||09:46 PM||||I don't know about the cross reference.<P>GM online lists the part for $19.24 plus shipping.<P>I would guess that BorgWarner made the same mistake as GM when they offered the part, I say cut your loses and go GM.||||reg||1
